spec.section:
### 6. Full SQL set: precise scope and executable diagnostics
**CHD production SQL set = the empty set.** The required memory transport has no SQL mutation, DDL, join, unique index, CAS or transaction endpoint in this design. The following is an internal-equivalent diagnostic, executable against synthetic JSONL only. It is not claimed to be a byte-for-byte copy of every optimized DuckBrain query branch. Pinned `src/duckdb/queries.ts` contains the real dynamic list/count/fused SQL; excerpts and the exact all-VARCHAR schema are attached below.
```sql -- D01: namespace JSONL relation; bind the file path as a parameter in the local probe. CREATE VIEW memory_rows AS SELECT * FROM read_json('fixture.jsonl', format='newline_delimited', ignore_errors=true, columns={id:'VARCHAR', key:'VARCHAR', domain:'VARCHAR', timestamp:'VARCHAR', valid_from:'VARCHAR', valid_until:'VARCHAR', author:'VARCHAR', action:'VARCHAR', embedding_text:'VARCHAR', attributes:'VARCHAR'});
-- D02: physical UUID tombstone reduction; does NOT resolve application rev. SELECT id,key,domain,timestamp,valid_from,valid_until,author,action,embedding_text,attributes FROM (SELECT *,row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY id ORDER BY try_cast(timestamp AS TIMESTAMP) DESC NULLS LAST) AS rn FROM memory_rows) WHERE rn=1 AND action <> 'tombstone' ORDER BY try_cast(timestamp AS TIMESTAMP) DESC NULLS LAST,id ASC;
-- D03: inspect, never assert success from this query alone; Go checks byte conflicts. SELECT key,try_cast(json_extract_string(embedding_text,'$.rev') AS BIGINT) AS app_rev, embedding_text FROM memory_rows WHERE action <> 'tombstone';
-- D04: actual optional FTS sidecar DDL from pinned src/search/index.ts:562. CREATE TABLE memories (id VARCHAR, key VARCHAR, domain VARCHAR, timestamp VARCHAR, valid_from VARCHAR, valid_until VARCHAR, author VARCHAR, action VARCHAR, embedding_text VARCHAR, attributes VARCHAR, raw_text VARCHAR, search_text VARCHAR); -- Extension-owned optional search setup, NOT run by CHD or this verification: -- INSTALL fts; LOAD fts; -- PRAGMA create_fts_index('memories', 'id', 'search_text'); ```
All file-path interpolation in diagnostics is trusted fixture setup. Application query values use transport encoding, not SQL string substitution. There is no `SELECT * FROM room_message`, `ON CONFLICT`, `BEGIN/COMMIT`, `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX`, `UPDATE ... WHERE rev=...`, or SQLite lease row in the production design.

### Appendix E — complete generated Go read-view definitions
These compile as a single package with the standard library. Schema validation, enum validation, presence-aware patching, canonicalization, writer fencing and publication are required separately. They are not fabricated existing CHD source.
